# The remote carries a commit this head does not. An autofix commit is exactly
# this shape: the bot pushes, the branch's own head stops being the pull
# request's head, and `## Head` now names a SHA no push will ever make current
# -- there is nothing to push. Refused, and the refusal cannot fire on the
# ordinary path, where a fresh commit always leaves HEAD ahead and never behind.
#
# <upstream-sha or -> <behind> <ahead> <wanted rc> <what the assertion says>
